SUMMARY:John Rock Loop Hike
DESCRIPTION:WNC Sierra Club\nJoin the WNC Sierra Club for a beautiful hike
  in the Pisgah National Forest. The John Rock Loop hike features around 1\
 ,100 feet of elevation gain up to a scenic overlook where we will have a s
 nack and rest. This hike is about 5.9 miles in length and will take us app
 roximately 3-4 hours. Be prepared for elevation gain and creek crossings. 
 Make sure to pack food and water to stay nourished and hydrated! Wear gear
  that you are comfortable hiking in and good shoes. It is also a good idea
  to have rain gear just to be safe. If you are feeling unwell and/or have 
 a fever\, please help us to keep everyone safe and healthy by waiting for 
 the next outing. Families\, friends\, and pets are all welcome. An adult m
 ust accompany all children. All dogs must remain on a leash and be friendl
 y to all.\n\nPlease register using this [Link to John Rock Loop Hike Regis
 tration.](https://act.sierraclub.org/events/details?formcampaignid=701Po00
 002DA0ZMIA1)\n\nYOU NEED TO EMAIL THE HIKE LEADER TO CONFIRM REGISTRATION 
 SPOT AND GET INFORMATION ABOUT THE MEETING SPOT!\n\nMarshall Heilig (Hike 
 Leader)\nemail: mdheilig03@gmail.com\ntext: 828.808.7512\n\nAmber Fox (Hik
 e Co-Leader)\namber.ahrens@hotmail.com
